Package: pitw
Title: PIT-Wasserstein Metrics for Diagnosing Dispersion Miscalibration
Version: 0.0.0.9001
Authors@R: 
    person("Rob", "Challen", , "rob.challen@bristol.ac.uk", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-5504-7768"))
Description: Implements the PIT-Wasserstein family of metrics for diagnosing
    dispersion miscalibration in probabilistic estimators. The package provides
    three nested metrics—B_pit (baseline), U_pit (bias-adjusted undirected), and
    D_pit (bias-adjusted signed, detecting overconfidence vs. underconfidence)—each
    with a significance test based on a large-sample reference distribution
    for independent predictions. Also provides batch scoring,
    CRPS calculation, simulation helpers, and diagnostic visualisation tools.
